<title>FRANCE: Subsidies - Who pays what to OECD farmers.</title>
<headline>Subsidies - Who pays what to OECD farmers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here is a league table of OECD agricultural subsidies in 1996, released in a new report.</p>
<p>The figures show subsidies measured as so-called Producer Subsidy Equivalents -- the cost of policies or inflated consumer prices which are most directly involved in helping farmers.</p>
<p>Countries are ranked by the 1996 percentage of these subsidies within the total value of each country's farm output.</p>
<p>						  1996(e)   1995(p)</p>
<p>1.  SWITZERLAND</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     5.49	5.97</p>
<p>	Percentage			     78	  80</p>
<p>2.  JAPAN (joint second)</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		    40.53     48.90</p>
<p>	Percentage			     71	  77</p>
<p>2.   NORWAY (joint second)</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     2.51	2.54</p>
<p>	Percentage			     71	  72</p>
<p>4.  ICELAND</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     0.12	0.13</p>
<p>	Percentage			     68	  74</p>
<p>5.  EUROPEAN UNION (15 countries)</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		    85.01     95.84</p>
<p>	Percentage			     43	  49</p>
<p>6.  TURKEY</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     3.67	3.43</p>
<p>	Percentage			     30	  31</p>
<p>7.  POLAND*</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     3.02	2.12</p>
<p>	Percentage			     28	  21</p>
<p>8.  CANADA</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     3.84	4.04</p>
<p>	Percentage			     22	  23</p>
<p>9.  UNITED STATES</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		    23.51     17.38</p>
<p>	Percentage			     16	  13</p>
<p>10. MEXICO*</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     1.95	0.35</p>
<p>	Percentage			     13	   3</p>
<p>11. HUNGARY*</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     0.46	0.58</p>
<p>	Percentage			     11	  16</p>
<p>12. CZECH REPUBLIC*</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     0.32	0.42</p>
<p>	Percentage			     10	  14</p>
<p>13. AUSTRALIA</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     1.19	1.26</p>
<p>	Percentage				9	   9</p>
<p>14. NEW ZEALAND</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		     0.14	0.15</p>
<p>	Percentage				3	   3</p>
<p>TOTAL OECD (see note)</p>
<p>	Total PSE ($bn)		   166.00    179.64</p>
<p>	Percentage			     36	  40</p>
<p>NOTES - The OECD total does not include the figures for four countries which have recently joined the organisation, marked with an asterisk. The OECD does not give any figures for its most recent member, South Korea.</p>
<p>(e) means estimate (p) means provisional.</p>
<p>Dollars are U.S. throughout.</p>
<p>Source, Agricultural Policies, Markets and Trade in OECD Countries -- Monitoring and Evaluation, 1997. Published by the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development, Paris.</p>
